From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] REJECTED dagu: maybe_post without waiting for Cogl sync_fd

Live A/B 2026-09-14: 108.1 Hz, gt50=5, max 225.5, B-kick-atomic-late 185 ms.
Worse than dri_flush-NOP baseline (109.7 / 5 / 116.6). Restored 0x1c43f4.

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18 50.1-0ubuntu2.2).

maybe_post_if_gl_finished() returns when the next frame is in the
render_source hash and sync.revents lacks G_IO_IN. On dagu that
fence is implicit-synced to the scanout BO, so nview runs on time
but maybe_post waits ~100 ms (Type B).

Post as soon as the previous frame is presented. GPU completion
belongs on IN_FENCE / KMS, not the UI thread.

Live ELF (objdump-checked):
  0x1c43f4  tbnz w0,#0,post  ->  b post

---
 src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c b/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
@@ -250,13 +250,7 @@ maybe_post_next_frame_if_gl_finished (CoglOnscreen *onscreen)
   if (frame == NULL)
     return;
 
-  if (render_source &&
-      g_hash_table_contains (render_source->frames, frame) &&
-      !meta_frame_native_is_ready (meta_frame_native_from_frame (frame)))
-    {
-      return;
-    }
-
   maybe_post_next_frame (onscreen);
 }
